      "totalDuration": "3 yrs 4 mos",
      "description": "Lead Engineer for Amazon Merch on Demand’s global fulfillment operations, including warehouse management systems, associate facing web and mobile applications, and backend order ingestion and processing services.\n\n• Set technical direction for business-critical systems supporting fulfillment centers operating around the clock.\n• Led the launch for Direct Film Transfer printing, enabling new product capabilities and licensed merchandise for the NBA, NFL, and NHL.\n• Led the launch of a new drinkware manufacturing process, enabling Merch on Demand to produce and fulfill printed tumblers.\n• Worked across warehouse software, mobile applications, backend services, and manufacturing integrations to support worldwide fulfillment operations.\n• Drove operational excellence for systems requiring high availability, rapid incident response, and continuous production support.",
      "insights": ""
     },
     {
      "title": "Software Engineer II - Merch on Demand Content Moderation",
      "locationName": "Seattle, WA · On-site",
      "timePeriod": {
       "startDate": {
        "month": 1,
        "year": 2020
       },
       "endDate": {
        "month": 4,
        "year": 2022
       }
      },
      "totalDuration": "2 yrs 4 mos",
      "description": "Led development of content moderation systems for Amazon Merch on Demand, a global print-on-demand business supporting a catalog of more than 550 million ASINs.\n\n• Scaled daily moderation capacity by 10x, from approximately 7 million to 70 million ASINs per day.\nExpanded the moderation platform to support launches in France, Italy, Spain, and Japan.\n• Improved the systems and workflows used to review and publish product listings at scale.\n• Owned technical delivery across backend services, data-processing workflows, and operational tooling.\n• Earned promotion to Senior Software Development Engineer based on technical leadership and impact within the content moderation organization.",
      "insights": ""
